  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt safe S1 incident reporting (24h serious, 5 business days other/customer) and a mandatory 8/100k S5 recall with prompt notices. S2 sets a 5% test-failure threshold but no automatic sales stop, requires customer access to numeric per-model results, and bars public publication; S3 allows a 6-year retrofit, and S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months."
